        },
        "subject": "LU-20557 llog: don't call llog_size() if rc is set",
        "message": "LU-20557 llog: don't call llog_size() if rc is set\n\nThe llog_cat_size_cb() calls llog_cat_process_common() which\nsets valid llog_handler only along with rc == 0, but\nthere is missing rc == 0 check before llog_size() call,\nso it uses NULL llog_handler.\n\nPatch adds explicit check for rc == 0\n\nSigned-off-by: Mikhail Pershin <mpershin@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: Ib89a5af05ed9910ee7704e1878f247f2590ce0c4\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
